-- The takanon's root (MMS-521): every takanon provision that speaks to an
-- item of the shared vocabulary (l4/lib/vocabulary.l4), the instruments it
-- includes (each describes itself in its own file), and what each claims
-- for a case. It is a `collection root` (l4/roots/precedence.l4): the
-- takanon speaks once on an item, so its ruling is that provision. The root
-- (l4/roots/root.l4) sets it against the agreements' and the circulars'
-- rulings by the takanon's own introduction.
--
-- It imports the whole takanon (MMS-538), every module under l4/takanon/;
-- the IMPORT block is written by tools/roots.py (--write-takanon-imports).
-- Of all they declare it names only the provisions that describe themselves
-- as instruments and their `according to` answers.

